{# ============================================================================
   SETTINGS — what is neither a shift nor a rule.

   PORTED FROM the design's configure.html as the design agent trimmed it
   (uhifadhi-web 8e422aa). TWO ROWS, and that is the whole page besides the
   statuses card. The default catchment and the late and vacancy thresholds
   are RULES on the Watches section, the shift vocabulary is named and
   coloured there too, and the ping interval is the AREA's, set on its Area
   settings and shown read-only on the Watches rules card. A fact with two
   editors is a fact that disagrees with itself the first time somebody uses
   the other one, so this page keeps only what nothing else holds.

   COVERAGE MANIFEST — every element of the drawn page.

   | element                       | type    | source                   | interaction      | status |
   |-------------------------------|---------|--------------------------|------------------|--------|
   | page subline, three fragments | chrome  | static                   | none             | done   |
   | h2.zone + subhead → Watches   | chrome  | static                   | door to Watches  | done   |
   | Settings card head + caption  | chrome  | static                   | none             | done   |
   | Off days on a tour            | control | AreaRosterSettings       | two-state switch | done   |
   | Leave approval                | control | AreaRosterSettings       | two-state switch | done   |
   | Discard / Save settings       | control | —                        | reload / write   | done   |
   | Check-in statuses card        | data    | the AREA's list          | none — read here | done   |
   | one .rstat per status         | data    | CheckInStatus            | none             | done   |
   | retired row, dimmed and kept  | state   | CheckInStatus            | none             | done   |
   | empty status list             | state   | the area offers none     | none             | done   |
   | catchment / thresholds        | —       | —                        | —                | ON Watches, ruled 20–21 sep |
   | ping interval                 | —       | —                        | —                | THE AREA'S: Area settings, shown read-only on Watches |
   | shift vocabulary row          | —       | —                        | —                | MOVED to Watches, ruled 21 sep |
   | .rstat re-order / edit / retire | —     | —                        | —                | NOT THIS MODULE'S: the area writes them |

   THE ONE "post" LEFT ON THIS PAGE IS THE AREA'S CHECK-IN STATUS — the
   `at_post` key, its "At post" label and the kind it carries. The key is
   issued once and every stored check-in holds it, the label is the area's
   to reword and not this module's, and the kind's wording is the area
   module's enum. It stays until the owner rules on it.
   ========================================================================== #}
{% extends '@UhifadhiRoster/configure/_frame.html.twig' %}

{# WHETHER THIS PERSON MAY CHANGE HOW THE AREA RUNS ITS ROSTER — the pair
   every write on this page carries. The page itself opens on the ground,
   so a reader sees the setup with every control disabled. #}
{% set mayManage = door('roster.configure', area) %}

{# THE DESIGN'S OWN SUBLINE, as fragments. #}
{% block shell_page_subtitle %}What this module cannot guess about this organization &middot; each answer a field, with a default and the consequence of choosing wrong &middot; shifts and rules live on Watches{% endblock %}

{% block roster_section %}
<h2 class="zone" id="settings">Settings</h2>
<p class="pgsub">What is neither a shift nor a rule &middot; shifts and the rules that read them are edited once, on <a href="{{ path(constant('Uhifadhi\\Roster\\Controller\\RosterConfigureController::WATCHES_ROUTE'), {uuid: area.uuid}) }}">Watches</a></p>

<form method="post" action="{{ path(constant('Uhifadhi\\Roster\\Controller\\RosterConfigureController::SAVE_SETTINGS_ROUTE'), {uuid: area.uuid}) }}">
    <input type="hidden" name="_token" value="{{ csrfToken }}">
    <div class="c rband">
        {# HEADER = IDENTITY ONLY, no door: ruled 2026-09-20. #}
        <div class="rb-hd">
            <span class="tab">Settings</span>
            <span class="rb-ttl">two answers &mdash; neither of them a shift or a rule &middot; each with the consequence of getting it wrong</span>
        </div>
        <div class="rb-body">

            <div class="rset">
                <span class="lb"><b>Off days on a tour</b><em>what an off day in a cycle produces</em></span>
                <span class="ct">
                    <span class="rsw">
                        <label class="{{ settings.offDayHasNoState ? 'on' : '' }}"><input type="radio" name="off_day_has_no_state" value="1" {{ settings.offDayHasNoState ? 'checked' : '' }} {{ mayManage ? '' : 'disabled' }}>no state</label>
                        <label class="{{ settings.offDayHasNoState ? '' : 'on' }}"><input type="radio" name="off_day_has_no_state" value="0" {{ settings.offDayHasNoState ? '' : 'checked' }} {{ mayManage ? '' : 'disabled' }}>no check-in</label>
                    </span>
                </span>
                <span class="why"><b>Default: no state.</b> A ranger stood down owes no check-in &middot; choose <i>no check-in</i> only where everyone owes one daily &mdash; it colours every rest day red.</span>
            </div>

            <div class="rset">
                <span class="lb"><b>Leave approval</b><em>a request, an approver, a state machine</em></span>
                <span class="ct">
                    <span class="rsw">
                        <label class="{{ settings.leaveApprovalShown ? '' : 'on' }}"><input type="radio" name="leave_approval_shown" value="0" {{ settings.leaveApprovalShown ? '' : 'checked' }} {{ mayManage ? '' : 'disabled' }}>off</label>
                        <label class="{{ settings.leaveApprovalShown ? 'on' : '' }}"><input type="radio" name="leave_approval_shown" value="1" {{ settings.leaveApprovalShown ? 'checked' : '' }} {{ mayManage ? '' : 'disabled' }}>on</label>
                    </span>
                </span>
                <span class="why"><b>Default: off.</b> The roster records an absence &middot; approval belongs to Team &middot; on adds a read-only state chip, nothing more.</span>
            </div>

            {# Save at the END of the form body, right-aligned — the house's
               own .staddrow, not a footer strip. #}
            {% if mayManage %}
                <div class="staddrow">
                    <span class="sp"></span>
                    <a class="btn sm" href="{{ path(constant('Uhifadhi\\Roster\\Controller\\RosterConfigureController::SETTINGS_ROUTE'), {uuid: area.uuid}) }}">Discard</a>
                    <button type="submit" class="cta">Save settings</button>
                </div>
            {% endif %}
        </div>
    </div>
</form>

{# THE CHECK-IN STATUSES A RANGER IS OFFERED are the AREA's list, not this
   module's. The design puts them on this page because this is where somebody
   configuring the roster looks for them — read here, written there. #}
<div style="height:12px"></div>
<div class="c rband">
    <div class="rb-hd">
        <span class="tab">Check-in statuses</span>
        <span class="rb-ttl">what a ranger is offered on the handset &middot; the <b>area&rsquo;s</b> list, read here and written there</span>
    </div>
    <div class="rb-body">
        {% for status in checkInStatuses %}
            <div class="rstat {{ status.isActive ? '' : 'off' }}">
                <span class="ord">{{ status.isActive ? loop.index : '—' }}</span>
                <span class="nm"><b>{{ status.label }}</b><span class="key">{{ status.key }}</span></span>
                <span class="kind">{{ status.kind.label }}</span>
                <span class="st">
                    {%- if status.isActive %}
                        offered on the handset
                    {%- else %}
                        retired &middot; kept, so a past day keeps its word
                    {%- endif %}
                </span>
            </div>
        {% else %}
            <div class="rfrag"><b>This area offers no check-in status</b><em>nothing to declare &middot; no presence to derive</em></div>
        {% endfor %}
    </div>
</div>
{% endblock %}
